30, 2013 to RMB944 million (US$152 million) in the same period in 2014. The increase was primarily due to an increase of RMB48 million in payroll and benefits expenses mainly relating to an increase in share-based compensation expense as a result of
the increase in fair value of our shares over the periods. The increase was also due to an increase of RMB19 million in depreciation expense which primarily related to the expansion of our corporate campuses. </P>
